{
  "title": "An intermediate vocabulary concentration meets the paper’s four threshold tests inconsistently on fresh synthetic seeds",
  "program": "G",
  "on_path": false,
  "hard": true,
  "statement": "An exploratory synthetic-only cross of the released Parisel baseline slot generator varied its vocabulary Zipf exponent and top-k successor count. At exponent 0.8 and top-k 30, all three exploratory seeds met each of the paper’s stated Currier A and B thresholds; the selected setting then met all four in 11/20 new seeds for each dialect (not necessarily the same seeds). On the 20 seeds, boundary end-to-start rate varied from 28.6% to 87.4%, MI from 0.335 to 0.492 bits, bilateral extremity was present in all runs, and boundary shape was Plateau in one, Intermediate in 13 and Zipfian in six. This is a noisy synthetic threshold check, not a held-out manuscript evaluation or a general refutation. The configuration was selected after inspecting eight settings; the fresh 20 seeds assess Monte Carlo stability, not an independent selection of model family or manuscript thresholds. The released generator’s tokenizer uses artificial units such as k2 and e2; at seed 1000, 7,441/37,000 generated words contain digits. Those outputs are not valid EVA submissions without a separately specified, validated encoding. Its explicit boundary-pair weighting also builds in directional structure, which must be disclosed and charged to model complexity.",
  "check": "Replicate the selected crossed setting with a valid one-to-one encoding of synthetic units, fit and evaluate class definitions on disjoint public and held-out manuscript pages without exposing the split, report uncertainty across generator seeds and dialects, verify the fixed tokenization and threshold conventions, and compare against simpler matched-complexity baselines. Use a reviewed scorer primitive; the current declarative scorer cannot evaluate these four author-specific signatures jointly. Do not infer a held-out result from this synthetic pilot.",
  "method": {
    "source": "https://github.com/labyrinthinesecurity/currier-signatures",
    "commit": "5d50101b57957bc7feaa002cec01d1ce5b2b11d9",
    "module": "signatures_v27.py",
    "input": "Synthetic data only; no manuscript file loaded. The four A/B ranges and MI minima are those printed in paper Tables 5 and 6.",
    "pilot": "37000 tokens per run; baseline bridge_size=2; cross vocab_zipf_alpha [0.0,0.4,0.8,1.2] with top_k [5,30], seeds [301,438,575]; 3 shuffles in evaluate_corpus_fast.",
    "followup": "After pilot selection, alpha=0.8, top_k=30; seeds 1000 through 1019 inclusive; otherwise identical. Count per-run E-to-S in [56,86]% A or [50,79]% B, at least one extreme start and end unit, MI >=0.29 A or >=0.25 B, and shape other than Plateau. These are the paper’s coarse thresholds; the per-run conjunction is an exploratory operationalization of its aggregate criterion.",
    "reproduction": "Import signatures_v27 as s. For each setting instantiate s.cfg_baseline(n_words=37000,bridge_size=2,top_k=k), set cfg.vocab_zipf_alpha=alpha, call s.evaluate_corpus_fast(cfg.generate(seed=seed),cfg.tokenizer,n_shuffles=3). Each run uses a new config or generates from the unchanged config and an independently seeded RNG.",
    "pilot_script_sha256": "687331a14c413642b2a14fe4c36dffea5ba15cf44dba2e43e1a3aae1ff2bbbb0",
    "followup_script_sha256": "13f5f6ba2d5a43a743c1f0bdf4f7de29849ff8796077a98b47c98032551f362d"
  },
